# Long original prose is content, not Python expression layout.
"""Lesson-specific teaching prose for every Swift guide.

Each lesson has six fields: ``run`` (what to paste first and which failure class to expect),
``trace_a`` and ``trace_b`` (a value-by-value trace of each worked example), ``regression``
(the smallest counterexample that separates the intended rule from the tempting wrong one),
``selfcheck`` (retrieval questions about this lesson's mechanism) and ``docs`` (which part of
the official documentation to read). render.py rejects a missing field, a field below its
word minimum, an em or en dash, and an opening reused by any other field or lesson. Shared
routines belong in ``courses/swift/STUDY-GUIDE.md``, not here.
"""

